{"title":"Subjectwise Test-3 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 DA Probability and Statistics","fileName":"031_Subjectwise Test-3 Part Syllabus GATE 2026 DA Probability and Statistics.html","branch":"DATA SCIENCE AND ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Data Science and AI","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A car manufacturing unit produces an average of 27 car per hour. What is the probability that no car is manufactured in a particular 3 hr period?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5d8ee389282c7c123df97863fee66bff3308d158.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f4f2717ec49b80072dca38bd761e501c69294834.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/413d7a009d4e4ab916d1b721f8d3924ee76e9fc4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/10cc8f4eb920eae96ca9ccf7091376f9ab019fa0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A random sample of 100 fluorescent light bulb has an average lifetime of 1570 hours, with a sample standard deviation of 120 hours. In two tailed hypothesis test at the 5% level of significance.<br />\nThe calculated test statistics is found to be <em>t</em> = –2.5.<br />\nFind the value of population mean (μ) that was assumed in the NULL hypothesis.<br />\n(Given <em>t</em><sub>0.025</sub> = 1.96</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1800</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 1600</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1575</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 1875</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a60c60c02d6968c51007a73dee88573fbbb94ec0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The heights of female students attending a GATE coaching have mean of 168.0 cm and a standard deviation of 4.5 cm. The heights can be modelled by a normal distribution. Find the probability that height of a randomly selected female student attending this coaching is less than 172.5 cm ________. (Upto 3 decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.841","high":"0.841"},"solution":"<p>0.841 [0.840 - 0.845]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/a0d7856b4be9749a73cf02b792a721014a75c53c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A certain random variable has the CDF:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/72e930a25c136db28af0a31e9949ec5b4f2c86bc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>The value of <em>P</em>(5 < <em>X</em> ≤ 7) is _______. (Rounded off to two decimal places)</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.24","high":"0.24"},"solution":"<p>0.24 [0.20 - 0.28]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/88740800a3f3378057eeb9ac09be351d33c7aaf4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following properties about cumulative distribution function <em>F<sub>X</sub></em>(<em>x</em>) of a random variable <em>X</em> is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/10488ffa92a94e986182b8985d3cd6b994a0abc7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f076eb0a52d1592ed579c4c5cc6e41615c26102f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/5ae0009b4cd70673340aeaec9