iv>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/da54fda83a84c7aacc2e7cf0dd6bcc2baeb3efbe.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/926914b7c6cc021beaa36a3f42729f6276795155.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A researcher claims that more than 65% of college students prefer online learning over in-person classes.<br />\nA previous study found that the proportion was 0.65.<br />\nIn a recent survey of <em>n</em> = 2500 students, <em>x</em> = 1700 said they prefer online learning.<br />\nWhich of the following hypothesis pairs should be used to test the claim?</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/616bff12bd4a526946472cfff8def2998cb5d28e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> a</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> b</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> c</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> d</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/bc20ec9f088dba5cdb621fc3d41111cd75e02532.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Consider 4 similar boxes A, B, C and D. A is empty, B contains one green and one blue ball,<br />\nC contains one red and one blue ball, and D contains one red and one green ball. We randomly<br />\nselect a box. <em>E</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>E</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>E</em><sub>3</sub> be the events that selected box contains red, green and blue ball respectively.<br />\nWhich of the following statements is/are incorrect?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>E</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>E</em><sub>2</sub> are independent events.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <em>E</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>E</em><sub>3</sub> are independent events.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <em>E</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>E</em><sub>3</sub> are independent events.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <em>E</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>E</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>E</em><sub>3</sub> are independent events.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/210b10777fb72377b42babef45fea9acab1a8c19.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":22,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A sample of size n = 16 has sample mean overline <img src=\"/media/8fd35529c576334fcfa2728ead717e4ee2df8a47.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> = 12.5<br />\nThe population mean is μ = 11.0 and the computed t-statistic is t = 2.0.<br />\nFind the sample Standard deviation s.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p>3.0</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/55e0ef30281b0d7f00005f178bfadf58ab962f85.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":23,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X<sub>n</sub></em> be a sequence of discrete random variable where</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b1e2bb332d7b24766f63824bb12dd6e52e67e866.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following statements are correct?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8e108a072ee3eefca970adff11370030787bfe26.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/b68f2efbd67f4c986ac65bd7dd6a715583462443.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4d73a1d5715242cdf5693a99545fdff5be28498d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/71796575d8274d4fc50f1b6d94ada896bad6280a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e7b545f7941f544881886fd0eb46201d93a97ce4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/10281ae79224d8724429efea6e7d66b78b7450f3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> are two Gaussian random variables with <em>E</em>(<em>X</em>) = <em>E</em>(<em>Y</em>) = 0 and <img src=\"/media/de73fb734d05eed3d9761a999d7d6233f8e36e62.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> and<br />\ncorrelation coefficient between X and Y is 0.25. Let the random variable W be defined as :</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/08c36ef0f76a473fa64c488cf36b7aea709d07b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>where α is a positive real constant. The value of α which makes <em>X</em> and <em>W</em> independent is</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 2</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/e901fb5ae10c61078a71d6657abada1b902af254.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 3</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/957c78364574920edb46a5b54a2b72fc6a71c327.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/bc9b4a2458907028b38e14fd7435be9c9ef31bfb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":25,"type":"NAT","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In a two-category experiment, the observed frequencies are 45 and 55. The expected frequency of category B is 50, and the chi-square statistic χ<sup>2</sup> is 2. Find the expected frequency for category A.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"54","high":"54"},"solution":"<p>54</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/e6101ef82e57f9cca879b1f06a6c9a5174419ed5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":26,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Suppose a factory has machine I, II and III that produce XYZ phones. The factory’s record shows that Machine I, II and III produce, respectively 2%, 1% and 3% defective XYZ phones. Out of total production, Machine I, II, and III produce, respectively 35%, 25% and 40% of all XYZ phones a XYZ phone is selected at random from the factor if given that phone is defective what is the conditional probability that it was produced by Machine III? [Upto 2 decimal places]</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.56","high":"0.56"},"solution":"<p>0.56 [0.55 - 0.56]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b5c92526843088c7fe72fd8ab2b96383c253c68a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":27,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A fair coin is tossed <em>n</em> times independently. Let the random variable <em>X</em> denote the number of times two consecutive head (HH) appear in the sequence of tosses.<br />\nWhat is the expected value of <em>X</em>, <em>E</em>(<em>X</em>)?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/27f83ac663ff614cfc2e66c0ea1f3368db91c941.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/1dc9e0b17be6924324e826d3b638e102df5323da.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f9c74c5f9882a1c2c5d044b1e3cce4c3631bf4de.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/23fb607bd760e1bf40856fe4dbd4b0e98bc68289.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":28,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The joint pdf of <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> is given by</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/db0ad634b15a397a6ee2c2864d4453138a54cb1b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>where a = 3 and b = 4. The value of constant k is _______.</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12","high":"12"},"solution":"<p>12</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5b914d7ae5254b9f2f56d381fb84d1279e265f1e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Two independent random variables <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> are identical and uniformly distributed in the range [0, 2]. The probability that min[<em>X</em>, <em>Y</em>] is less than 1 is equal to _________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.75","high":"0.75"},"solution":"<p>0.75 [0.74 - 0.76]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/646ef993eee658de1eadfa6a6d31a10acd9f34ba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Suppose that a book of 1200 pages contains 80 printing mistakes. Assume that these errors are randomly distributed throughout the book and x, the number of errors per page has a Poisson distribution. The probability that 15 pages selected at random will be free of error is _________.<br />\n(correct upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.37","high":"0.37"},"solution":"<p>0.37 [0.35 - 0.38]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/bd761e2da774629890dabb53c9f17361221e846f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A fair six-sided die is rolled twice. Let the outcomes of the first and second rolls be denoted by <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em>.</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5dfa61c3fe885b8a6ddb04468c97c09aa5f67e12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following is incorrect?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/233acbaa5aac8f253d5cab53c6f2261047f4d31e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/cb2f0991973d2fe63a7e6036430a39e4fc73c6e1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/9bbbced735dd543af55c93b65bb19cb0ca7e7292.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4b5fa13facb9a1606c9d2865551571ba022d24f0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/885d1266579038152dd220bb1490cf8810ffabc3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider four students in a class, and their marks in exam was 40, 50, 60 and 70. The Standard deviation of this data set is ________. (Upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"11.18","high":"11.18"},"solution":"<p>11.18 [11.00 - 12.00]</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/411b8949a73dc4e24bb77b8e9e871d29af19ef9d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The joint probability density function of two random variables <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> is given by,</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f6bb3ad8058b97120bc1c3581f61406ba3cfb266.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>The value of <em>k</em> will be</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/4b059c8fb01a11f79fcd6a79f070046374521f52.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8abc7404d07397262cc39e82d10764d036ac1985.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/a1bdcc43c8450f1e3857e1cbde91d9d531005bef.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f318d16f06bc45d7088187ede2cef8591a5c10a7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/1ab48bc976db1d3d7efe1aa952f76f459a106357.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"}],"questionCount":33,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:08.036Z"}